flint test: run `test` blocks

Usage:
  flint test [options] [file.fl]

  Runs every `test "name" { ... }` block of the file and of the modules it imports; in a
  package, of every .fl file. Each test runs in its own process, so a panic fails only
  that test. The exit status is 1 when a test failed.

Options:
  -O0, -O2             no optimization, with debugging aids (default); or optimized
  --overflow=<mode>    integer overflow: trap (default) or wrap
  --color=<when>       colored output: auto (default), always or never
  -h, --help           show this help

  Bounds, null, cast and division checks are always on: only 'unsafe' removes them.

Examples:
  flint test parser.fl
  flint test                    (in a package)
